From a0552cf32e8ab74f78956415f9c09c8fecef4faf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:59:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Use every Camera1 feature of the HAL, One UI style layout

The libhybris camera compatibility layer covers only part of the Camera1
parameters. libcamx.so (src/camx/camx.cpp) is a small bionic-side library,
built with clang for the Android target and loaded with android_dlopen, that
works on the compatibility layer's own CameraControl after checking its
layout at runtime (the listener field must hold the pointer the app passed).
It sets any Camera1 key (exposure compensation, AE/AWB lock, anti-flicker),
dumps the full parameter set and installs a proxy CameraListener that keeps
the face detection metadata the compatibility layer drops.

On top of it:
- every camera the HAL exposes, with a One UI zoom pill whose lens factors
  come from the field of view (.5x ultra wide on the Galaxy S10+) and a
  logarithmic zoom slider
- pro and pro video modes (EV, white balance, focus mode, AE/AWB lock),
  hyperlapse, QR in a "more" grid; settings sheet with scene/HDR, effects,
  anti-flicker, face detection, geotagging, every photo size, JPEG quality,
  video frame rate, H.264/HEVC, encoder and bit rate
- tap to focus and meter, face boxes mapped with the renderer's geometry
- the HAL's JPEG is saved as-is (EXIF orientation, GPS, quality kept) with
  the rotation passed to the camera instead of re-encoding a QImage
- user choices are stored per camera and applied again after reconnecting
- Polish translation

Fixes found on the way:
- viewfinder shader used abs() on an int, which GLSL ES 1.00 lacks and the
  Mali driver rejects: black viewfinder
- the camera was opened twice at startup, the second connection lost the
  continuous focus mode; mode defaults are now applied after every switch
- the zoom index started at 1 (1.07x) while the HAL starts at 0
- 4032x1908 video is refused (encoder capped at 3840 wide, CameraSource
  rejects 3840x1908), so sizes above 3840x2160 are not offered
- the window was mapped at 500x500 and resized later
- the renderer drew with its default 1920x1080 until the first size change

Signed-off-by: Artur <ganggg111@gmail.com>
